-- title:
--   Reducedness of the closed fibre from reduced stalks modulo mathfrak m_A
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a commutative local ring, let $X$ be a scheme, and let `toBase` $: X \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ be a morphism of schemes. Assume that for every point $x$ of $X$ whose image under the underlying continuous map of `toBase` is the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} A$, the quotient of the stalk $\mathcal O_{X,x}$ by the ideal generated by the image of the maximal ideal $\mathfrak m_A$ under the structure map $A \to \mathcal O_{X,x}$ — realised as the composite of the inverse of the isomorphism $A \cong \Gamma(\operatorname{Spec} A, \mathcal O)$, the map on global sections induced by `toBase`, and the germ map $\Gamma(X,\mathcal O_X) \to \mathcal O_{X,x}$ — is a reduced ring. Then the fibre product of `toBase` with $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the residue map $A \to A/\mathfrak m_A$ is a reduced scheme. Thus the hypothesis is reducedness of the rings $\mathcal O_{X,x}/\mathfrak m_A\mathcal O_{X,x}$ at the points of $X$ over the closed point, and the conclusion is reducedness of the closed fibre $X \times_{\operatorname{Spec} A} \operatorname{Spec} \kappa(A)$ as a scheme.
--
--   This is the standard criterion identifying the closed fibre over a local base as the closed subscheme cut out by $\mathfrak m_A$, together with the fact that a scheme is reduced precisely when all of its stalks are reduced. It is used to establish reducedness of the special fibre of a semistable model, via [`AlgebraicCurve.SemistableModel.isReduced_pullback_residue_of_level`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.SemistableModel.isReduced_pullback_residue_of_level).
